# Does Creature::Phase name the plane the character really enters? Read by
# tools/repro_phase_plane_name.sh, bead inc-ef99.
#
# DEFECT (fixed): Phasing boots grant CA_PHASE with pval 2 = PHASE_ASTRAL
# (lib/m_items.irh:3978) yet their Desc says ethereal plane. The repro now
# requires the boots to grant PHASE_ETHEREAL and the printed name to match.
#
# fact: character -- fixture orc-barbarian-seed1-opt0822 (INCURSION_LOAD)
# fact: settings -- INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat
# fact: the item -- wizard Item Acquisition, boots walked to "Boots of Phasing"
# fact: item level / plus -- typed 3 at the acquisition prompt
# fact: the phase value -- AI_BOOTS Effect "Phasing" pval PHASE_ETHEREAL (data, not a roll)
# fact: no roll is read -- use ability 'u' always succeeds (Creature::Phase)
# fact: text matched -- fixed strings in src/Skills.cpp, not seed-decided
#
# Observations: the message "You phase into the ..." (@dump:after-phase) and
# the boots' own page, which names the plane from the stored value
# (src/Help.cpp:3857) (@dump:boots-page).

w
y
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*20
@until "Boots of Phasing" DOWN
DOWN                    # the middle row is the selected one: step onto it
ENTER
3
ENTER
@dump:boots-acquired    # the acquisition wears them: slot k reads Boots of Phasing
k
x
@dump:boots-page        # examine the boots: the page names the plane from the stored value
ESC
ESC
u
@dump:use-menu
@choose "Phase"
@dump:after-phase       # the message line is the oracle: "You phase into the <name>."
w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
@until "PHASED" PGDN
@dump:stati-phased      # wizard Creature::Dump prints the real plane: Val:PHASE_xxx
